**Definition 3.2 (the two typed languages).** The retained pair is
$\sigma=(\mu,w)$, where $w$ is the entire actually imported history frame.
If $\mu=0$, call the unchanged legacy parser and ARC §8 binder: successful
frames are exactly its $111\,U(\ell)\,U(m)U(z)U(s)$ with
$\ell=|U(m)U(z)U(s)|$ and its existing occurrence/phase/range checks.
All complete old malformed tags/payloads and old range/occurrence failures
retain their first-detecting legacy reason and raw-frame interpretation.

If $\mu=1$, require $w=111\,U(\ell)P$, exact $\ell$ payload bits,
and exhaustion. Parse one literal payload bit. On zero use ReadUnary
once and require exhaustion: $P=0U(t)$. On one use ReadUnary twice and
require exhaustion: $P=1U(m)U(t)$. Every unary must terminate. A missing
field, extra suffix, wrong tag or length mismatch is MalformedRecovery.
A finite invalid range is binding/range failure; an absent authentic
source occurrence is NoOccurrence. An unfinished physical length or payload
remains actual ingress, without an invented completed rejection. No source
frame bit serves as HistoryMode, and no first history-header bit is removed
to supply it.

